{
  "about": "work: links in a reply on the phones and the website (docs/protocol.md, \"Links into the thread\"). op escape: agents write [tests pass](work:npm test), and a destination with a space isn't a link to a markdown parser, so the destinations are escaped first; expect.links is what each link destination with no space left in it reads as after escaping (null for a web page), in order, so one left alone in a code span isn't there. op find: the step a work link in message `from` (null: the card of asks, so the latest turn) means: the latest in that message's turn whose words have the quote, lowercased, spaces as one and /Users/<name> as ~, and never the link's own message or a summary; expect.step is its seq or null. busy: the last turn is still going. The iPhone (ThreadLinks), Android (ThreadLinks) and the website (web/src/thread-links.ts). The desktop app has its own WorkLinks (desktop/core/src/reducer/work_links.rs), which scores a step's command, fields and output and is held to the frozen Mac app's by the golden files, so it isn't here.",
  "platforms": ["ios", "android", "web"],
  "cases": [
    {"name": "the destinations agents write are escaped", "input": {"op": "escape", "markdown": "and that's [landed on main](work:Commit, land, retire the old shared simulator) as `ec865ff`."}, "expect": {"links": [{"kind": "step", "value": "Commit, land, retire the old shared simulator"}]}},
    {"name": "web links and paths are left alone", "input": {"op": "escape", "markdown": "[x](https://a.b/c) and [y](/a/b.md)"}, "expect": {"links": [null, null]}},
    {"name": "an escaped destination stays as it was", "input": {"op": "escape", "markdown": "[done](work:npm%20test)"}, "expect": {"links": [{"kind": "step", "value": "npm test"}]}},
    {"name": "a link in a code span is left as written", "input": {"op": "escape", "markdown": "Write `[a](work:npm test)` like that, [b](work:npm test)"}, "expect": {"links": [{"kind": "step", "value": "npm test"}]}},
    {"name": "a quote can have brackets in it", "input": {"op": "escape", "markdown": "[a](work:npm test (unit)) next"}, "expect": {"links": [{"kind": "step", "value": "npm test (unit)"}]}},
    {"name": "a thread link is escaped too", "input": {"op": "escape", "markdown": "see [that](thread:a1b2c3d4)"}, "expect": {"links": [{"kind": "thread", "value": "a1b2c3d4"}]}},
    {"name": "a work link finds its step in its own turn", "input": {"op": "find", "quote": "commit,  LAND", "from": 9, "busy": false, "rows": [{"seq": 1, "role": "user", "text": "First"}, {"seq": 2, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 3, "role": "assistant", "text": "All done.", "summary": true}, {"seq": 4, "role": "user", "text": "Second"}, {"seq": 5, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 6, "role": "assistant", "text": "Now the risky part."}, {"seq": 7, "role": "tool", "text": "Commit, land, retire the old simulator"}, {"seq": 8, "role": "tool", "text": "Edited ~/dev/a.swift"}, {"seq": 9, "role": "assistant", "text": "- [Landed](work:Commit, land)\n- [Tested](work:run the tests)", "summary": true}]}, "expect": {"step": 7}},
    {"name": "in both turns, the link's own turn's", "input": {"op": "find", "quote": "Run the tests", "from": 9, "busy": false, "rows": [{"seq": 1, "role": "user", "text": "First"}, {"seq": 2, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 3, "role": "assistant", "text": "All done.", "summary": true}, {"seq": 4, "role": "user", "text": "Second"}, {"seq": 5, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 6, "role": "assistant", "text": "Now the risky part."}, {"seq": 7, "role": "tool", "text": "Commit, land, retire the old simulator"}, {"seq": 8, "role": "tool", "text": "Edited ~/dev/a.swift"}, {"seq": 9, "role": "assistant", "text": "- [Landed](work:Commit, land)\n- [Tested](work:run the tests)", "summary": true}]}, "expect": {"step": 5}},
    {"name": "an earlier turn's link finds its own turn's step", "input": {"op": "find", "quote": "Run the tests", "from": 3, "busy": false, "rows": [{"seq": 1, "role": "user", "text": "First"}, {"seq": 2, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 3, "role": "assistant", "text": "All done.", "summary": true}, {"seq": 4, "role": "user", "text": "Second"}, {"seq": 5, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 6, "role": "assistant", "text": "Now the risky part."}, {"seq": 7, "role": "tool", "text": "Commit, land, retire the old simulator"}, {"seq": 8, "role": "tool", "text": "Edited ~/dev/a.swift"}, {"seq": 9, "role": "assistant", "text": "- [Landed](work:Commit, land)\n- [Tested](work:run the tests)", "summary": true}]}, "expect": {"step": 2}},
    {"name": "the card of asks has no message, so the latest turn", "input": {"op": "find", "quote": "Run the tests", "from": null, "busy": false, "rows": [{"seq": 1, "role": "user", "text": "First"}, {"seq": 2, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 3, "role": "assistant", "text": "All done.", "summary": true}, {"seq": 4, "role": "user", "text": "Second"}, {"seq": 5, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 6, "role": "assistant", "text": "Now the risky part."}, {"seq": 7, "role": "tool", "text": "Commit, land, retire the old simulator"}, {"seq": 8, "role": "tool", "text": "Edited ~/dev/a.swift"}, {"seq": 9, "role": "assistant", "text": "- [Landed](work:Commit, land)\n- [Tested](work:run the tests)", "summary": true}]}, "expect": {"step": 5}, "differs": {"web": "findStep needs the link's message: the website has no card of asks with work links."}},
    {"name": "a line the agent wrote is a step", "input": {"op": "find", "quote": "risky part", "from": 9, "busy": false, "rows": [{"seq": 1, "role": "user", "text": "First"}, {"seq": 2, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 3, "role": "assistant", "text": "All done.", "summary": true}, {"seq": 4, "role": "user", "text": "Second"}, {"seq": 5, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 6, "role": "assistant", "text": "Now the risky part."}, {"seq": 7, "role": "tool", "text": "Commit, land, retire the old simulator"}, {"seq": 8, "role": "tool", "text": "Edited ~/dev/a.swift"}, {"seq": 9, "role": "assistant", "text": "- [Landed](work:Commit, land)\n- [Tested](work:run the tests)", "summary": true}]}, "expect": {"step": 6}},
    {"name": "a path as the agent wrote it finds the step's ~", "input": {"op": "find", "quote": "/Users/alex/dev/a.swift", "from": 9, "busy": false, "rows": [{"seq": 1, "role": "user", "text": "First"}, {"seq": 2, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 3, "role": "assistant", "text": "All done.", "summary": true}, {"seq": 4, "role": "user", "text": "Second"}, {"seq": 5, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 6, "role": "assistant", "text": "Now the risky part."}, {"seq": 7, "role": "tool", "text": "Commit, land, retire the old simulator"}, {"seq": 8, "role": "tool", "text": "Edited ~/dev/a.swift"}, {"seq": 9, "role": "assistant", "text": "- [Landed](work:Commit, land)\n- [Tested](work:run the tests)", "summary": true}]}, "expect": {"step": 8}},
    {"name": "words found nowhere find no step", "input": {"op": "find", "quote": "npm run nothing", "from": 9, "busy": false, "rows": [{"seq": 1, "role": "user", "text": "First"}, {"seq": 2, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 3, "role": "assistant", "text": "All done.", "summary": true}, {"seq": 4, "role": "user", "text": "Second"}, {"seq": 5, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 6, "role": "assistant", "text": "Now the risky part."}, {"seq": 7, "role": "tool", "text": "Commit, land, retire the old simulator"}, {"seq": 8, "role": "tool", "text": "Edited ~/dev/a.swift"}, {"seq": 9, "role": "assistant", "text": "- [Landed](work:Commit, land)\n- [Tested](work:run the tests)", "summary": true}]}, "expect": {"step": null}},
    {"name": "a link doesn't find itself in its own summary", "input": {"op": "find", "quote": "Landed", "from": 9, "busy": false, "rows": [{"seq": 1, "role": "user", "text": "First"}, {"seq": 2, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 3, "role": "assistant", "text": "All done.", "summary": true}, {"seq": 4, "role": "user", "text": "Second"}, {"seq": 5, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 6, "role": "assistant", "text": "Now the risky part."}, {"seq": 7, "role": "tool", "text": "Commit, land, retire the old simulator"}, {"seq": 8, "role": "tool", "text": "Edited ~/dev/a.swift"}, {"seq": 9, "role": "assistant", "text": "- [Landed](work:Commit, land)\n- [Tested](work:run the tests)", "summary": true}]}, "expect": {"step": null}},
    {"name": "a turn still going searches its lines so far", "input": {"op": "find", "quote": "run the tests", "from": 3, "busy": true, "rows": [{"seq": 1, "role": "user", "text": "Go"}, {"seq": 2, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 3, "role": "assistant", "text": "[Ran](work:run the tests)"}]}, "expect": {"step": 2}},
    {"name": "a turn still going with no such line finds none", "input": {"op": "find", "quote": "nothing", "from": 3, "busy": true, "rows": [{"seq": 1, "role": "user", "text": "Go"}, {"seq": 2, "role": "tool", "text": "Run the tests"}, {"seq": 3, "role": "assistant", "text": "[Ran](work:run the tests)"}]}, "expect": {"step": null}},
    {"name": "a turn with no working finds nothing", "input": {"op": "find", "quote": "nothing", "from": 2, "busy": false, "rows": [{"seq": 1, "role": "user", "text": "Hi"}, {"seq": 2, "role": "assistant", "text": "[Hello](work:nothing)"}]}, "expect": {"step": null}}
  ]
}
